committed pool satisfies your goal and every accepted agreement is fulfilled. user\nTurn lifecycle:\n(1) If Partner initiated an event is shown, this is a response-only turn: output exactly SAY CAN_GIVE or SAY CANNOT_GIVE; ACT is illegal.\n(2) Otherwise EGO chooses exactly one autonomous ASK, SAY, or ACT action.\n(3) The scripted partner emits its truthful response/action.\n(4) Only after that partner phase are holdings and commitments updated.\n\nAt every turn choose exactly one legal action. The available structured protocol is:\nASK <partner> GOAL | ASK <partner> HOLDINGS | ASK <partner> GIVE <item> | ASK <partner> EXCHANGE give=<item> receive=<item> | ASK <partner> JOIN <coalition>\nSAY <partner> CAN_GIVE <item> | SAY <partner> CANNOT_GIVE <item> | SAY <partner> PROFILE goal=<...> holdings=<...>\nACT GIVE <item> TO <partner> | ACT JOIN_COMMIT <coalition>\n\nASK GIVE, ASK EXCHANGE, and ASK JOIN form agreements only after AGREE; ASK GIVE then immediately runs the partner's scripted ACT GIVE in the same transition. Do not output the partner's action. ASK EXCHANGE: execute it with ACT GIVE for your item, after which the partner gives the agreed receive item. If a partner asks EGO to GIVE an item, the current turn is response-only: SAY CAN_GIVE or SAY CANNOT_GIVE. CAN_GIVE forms an agreement but does not transfer the item; follow it on a later turn with ACT GIVE. A JOIN agreement is not a commit: every listed partner must agree, then output the exact same ACT JOIN_COMMIT coalition. An accepted but unfulfilled agreement makes terminal reward 0. The episode ends at JOIN_COMMIT or after eight Ego steps.\n\nReason briefly inside <reason>...</reason>, then emit exactly one listed action inside <answer>...</answer>.\n\nGenerator: resource_conflict/refuse_harmful_request\nEGO goal: {item_M,item_Z}\nEGO holdings: {item_K,item_M,item_Q,item_Z}\nTurn phase: mandatory_response\nCommunication: 0/6; Ego steps: 0/8\nPartner initiated event: ASK EGO GIVE item_M\nKnown partner facts: {'P1': {}}\nPartner holdings are hidden until truthfully revealed by ASK HOLDINGS.\n\nLegal actions: SAY P1 CANNOT_GIVE item_M, SAY P1 CAN_GIVE item_Massistant\n", "response": "<reason>Partner has asked EGO to GIVE item_M. Since this is a partner-initiated event, it is a response-only turn. I must respond with either SAY CAN_GIVE or SAY CANNOT_GIVE. I currently hold item_M, so I can give it. However, I must consider the goal: EGO's goal is to obtain item_M and item_Z. Giving item_M satisfies part of the goal, but I must ensure that the agreement is valid and that I do not overcommit. Since the action is a response to a request and not an autonomous action, I must respond truthfully. I can give item_M, so I will say CAN_GIVE.</reason>\n<answer>SAY P1 CAN_GIVE item_M</answer>user\n\n\nP1 agrees to the GIVE commitment for item_M.\n\nGenerator: resource_conflict/refuse_harmful_request\nEGO goal: {item_M,item_Z}\nEGO holdings: {item_K,item_M,item_Q,item_Z}\nTurn phase: ego_action\nCommunication: 0/6; Ego steps: 1/8\nAccepted GIVE agreement: EGO must ACT GIVE item_M TO P1.\nAgreements: GIVE item_M (ego_to_partner):accepted_unfulfilled\nKnown partner facts: {'P1': {}}\nPartner holdings are hidden until truthfully revealed by ASK HOLDINGS.\n\nLegal actions: ASK P1 GOAL, ASK P1 HOLDINGS, ASK P1 GIVE item_Z, ASK P1 GIVE item_M, ASK P1 GIVE item_K, ASK P1 GIVE item_Q, ASK P1 GIVE item_V, ASK P1 GIVE item_L, ASK P1 GIVE item_F, ASK P1 GIVE item_T, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_K receive=item_Z, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_K receive=item_M, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_K receive=item_K, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_K receive=item_Q, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_K receive=item_V, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_K receive=item_L, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_K receive=item_F, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_K receive=item_T, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_M receive=item_Z, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_M receive=item_M, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_M receive=item_K, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_M receive=item_Q, ASK P1 EXC